body.translated_text:
The self indeed is the lord of the self — who else could be the lord?
By the self alone is merit made, by the self alone one is purified;
by the self alone is evil done, by the self one is defiled — thus it is said.

A bundle of formations (<s>saṃskāra</s>) indeed proceeds in continuity;
this is just like something created by illusion (<s>māyā</s>), a deception of the deluded.
It is like a thorn lodged in the heart, beset with enemies;
there is nothing here that has substance — thus it is said.
